# Added in v0.42.0 — the audit's FND-003 and REPO-014.
#
# **What this file does NOT do here, and why it matters.** The ruleset has
# `require_code_owner_review: false`, and turning it on would break this repository:
# the only code owner is also the only person who opens pull requests, and GitHub does
# not let an author approve their own PR. Enabling it would block every merge,
# including this one. So this file documents ownership; it does not gate anything.
#
# What it *does* do: GitHub requests the owner as a reviewer on every PR, and the
# paths below make it visible which changes touch the verification surface. That is
# worth having even when the answer is always the same person — a reviewer reading a
# diff that touches `scripts/` or `.github/` should know that is the surface protecting
# everything else.

# Default: everything.
*                             @Er-Sajan-PLG

# The verification surface. A change here can weaken the gate that protects
# everything else, so it is named separately rather than left to the default.
/.github/                     @Er-Sajan-PLG
/eslint.config.mjs            @Er-Sajan-PLG
/package.json                 @Er-Sajan-PLG
/scripts/                     @Er-Sajan-PLG

# The sourced requirements and the schema they are validated against.
/data/requirements.json       @Er-Sajan-PLG
/docs/REQUIREMENTS-SCHEMA.md  @Er-Sajan-PLG
